rt parking area, turn left down to a primitive boat ramp.\n\n**Take Out:**  From Interstate 70 take the Westwater exit.   The ranger station and launch ramp is about 9 miles from the freeway.\n\n**Other Information Sources:**\n\nBLM, Grand Junction District, 2815 H Road, Grand Junction, CO 81501; 303-244-1480 begin\\_of\\_the\\_skype\\_highlighting303-244-1480end\\_of\\_the\\_skype\\_highlighting begin\\_of\\_the\\_skype\\_highlighting\n\n[BLM - Ruby/Horsethief information](http://www.blm.gov/co/st/en/nca/mcnca/recreation/Boating.html)\n\n[BLM - Ruby/Horsethief boating rules](http://www.blm.gov/co/st/en/nca/mcnca/recreation/Boating/Ruby-Horsethief_Boating_Information.html)\n\n[Colorado River Ruby-Horsethief Brochure](http://www.blm.gov/co/st/en/nca/mcnca/recreation/Boating/colorado_river_ruby-horsethief.html) pdf\n\n[Mountain Wayfarer blog](http://users.frii.com/uliasz/wayfarer/ruby_canyon.htm)\n\nReaches of the Colorado River:\n\n[01\\. Hot Sulphur Springs to Hwy 40 bridge (Byers Canyon)](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/377) (CO, IV)\n\n[02\\. Gore Canyon](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/378) (CO, IV-V)\n\n[03\\. Pumphouse campground to Rancho Del Rio (Pumphouse)](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/379) (CO, III)\n\n[04\\. Hanging Lake Exit 125 (I-70) to Shoshone Power Plant Exit 123 (I-70) (Barrel Springs)](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/380) (CO, IV-V \\[V+\\])\n\n[05\\. Shoshone Power Plant, Exit 123 (I-70) to Grizzly Creek, Exit 121 (I-70) (Shoshone)](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/4260) (CO, III-IV)\n\n[06\\. Cameo Dam (Big Sur / Lucky 7)](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/4261) (CO, III)\n\n[07\\. Loma to Westwater (Ruby / Horsethief Canyons)](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/381) (CO-UT, II)\n\n[08\\. Westwater to Rose Ranch (Westwater Canyon)](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1840) (UT, I-IV)\n\n[09\\. Cisco (Rose Ranch) to Moab (Professor Valley)](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1841) (UT, I-III)\n\n[10\\. Moab to Powell Reservoir (Cataract Canyon)](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1842) (UT, I-IV)\n\n[11\\. Lees Ferry to Lake Mead (Grand Canyon)](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/114) (AZ, I-V)\n\n[12\\. Black Canyon](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/3190) (AZ-NV, I)","averageGradient":"7","maxGradient":"0","length":"24.9","correlations":[{"reachID":"381","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":"Optimal flow range (flows based on 2014 Colorado Basin Flow Study). ","highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"2500","beginMediumRunnable":"4000","beginHighRunnable":"20000","endHighRunnable":"50000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"COLORADO RIVER NEAR COLORADO-UTAH STATE LINE","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"09163500","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"1860","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"2.77","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"39.1327434","longitude":"-109.02707585"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/09163500","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/09163500/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":"Previous Flowbands: \nRange of Boatable Flows (R0-R9): 2500 - 50000 cfs  Comment: Range of flows defined by 2014 Flow-Study. For some craft-types, flows may be runnable outside this range.\nMedium Runnable (R4-R6): 4000 - 20000 cfs  